{"cuisine/taoist-diet":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/taoist-diet","n":"Taoist diet","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in China","intro":[["While there are many historical and modern schools of Taoism with different teachings on the subject, many Taoist priests regard their  diet as extremely important to their physical, mental and spiritual health in one way or another, especially where the amount of qi in the food is concerned."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"taoist-diet"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taoist_diet"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"A Taoist Cookbook: With Meditations Taken from the Laozi Daode Jing","ref":"cookbook/a-taoist-cookbook-with-meditations-taken-from-the-laozi-daode-jing","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Michael R. Saso","note":"Vegetarian recipes paired with readings from the Daode Jing, by a scholar of Taoist religion.","url":"","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"ingredient/pilaf":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pilaf","n":"Pilaf","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Pilaf is a rice dish, or in some regions, a wheat dish, whose recipe usually involves cooking in stock or broth, adding spices, and other ingredients such as vegetables and meat, and employing some technique for achieving cooked grains that do not adhere."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pilaf"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilaf"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Iranian cuisine","cuisine/iranian-cuisine",[["Chelow kabab","dish/chelow-kabab"]]],["Yoshoku","cuisine/yoshoku"