arious theories."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-volga-rice"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volga_rice"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Yoshoku","cuisine/yoshoku"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Breaded cutlet","ingredient/breaded-cutlet"],["Fried rice","ingredient/fried-rice"],["Omelette","ingredient/omelette"],["Omurice","ingredient/omurice"],["Tonkatsu","ingredient/tonkatsu"]]},{"h":"More from Yoshoku","links":[["Chicken katsu","dish/chicken-katsu"],["Cream stew","dish/cream-stew"],["Doria (food)","dish/doria-food"],["Hayashi rice","dish/hayashi-rice"],["Menchi-katsu","dish/menchi-katsu"],["Naporitan","dish/naporitan"],["Rengatei","dish/rengatei"],["Tonkatsu","dish/tonkatsu"]]}]},"dish/xiaolongbao":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/xiaolongbao","n":"Xiaolongbao","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Xiaolongbao is a type of Chinese tangbao (汤包; 湯包), traditionally prepared in a xiaolong, a small bamboo steaming basket. Xiaolongbao is generally believed to have originated in Shanghai."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-xiaolongbao"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xiaolongbao"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"],["Taiwan cuisine","cuisine/taiwan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Auricularia heimuer","ingredient/auricularia-heimuer"],["Flour dough","ingredient/flour-dough"],["Gelatin","ingredient/gelatin"],["Lard","ingredient/lard"],["Napa cabbage","ingredient/napa-cabbage"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Shiitake","ingredient/shiitake"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","ref":"site/thewoksoflife-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true},{"na